  "title": "Tama",
  "creator": "CrossFit",
  "description": "An 800 m single-arm barbell farmers carry, 31 toes-to-bar, 31 push-ups and 31 front squats; a 400 m carry at a heavier bar, 31 toes-to-bar, 31 push-ups and 31 hang power cleans; then a 200 m carry at the heaviest bar, for time. Honours New Zealand Army Cpl. Luke Tamatea, killed by a roadside bomb in Bamyan Province, Afghanistan, in 2012. Carrying a barbell one-handed is awkward on purpose; switch hands as needed.",
